   121	## Units of analysis and intervals
   122	
   123	- D1/D3: the star is the unit. Wilson 95% on unweighted proportions; plain
   124	  Wilson on the negatives class (weights cancel); survey bootstrap for PPV;
   125	  ESS-Wilson only for other descriptive weighted proportions, labeled
   126	  approximate.
   127	- D2: the TESS target (TIC) is the CLUSTER; inference is CONDITIONAL on the
   128	  frozen window assignment (report unique window count and reuse table —
   129	  windows repeat across targets, and a target-only bootstrap does not
   130	  represent the 928-window frame; stated as a limitation).
   131	  Estimator: per-target mean over its replicates within a scenario/stratum;
   132	  aggregate = equal-weight mean over the 103 targets (a scenario mix, NOT
   133	  the 928-window frame). Bootstrap: resample the 103 TICs with replacement
   134	  (B = 2000, frozen seed 20260830), carrying ALL of a resampled target's
   135	  replicates, paired census/L-S outcomes, phases, and scenario results
   136	  jointly; identical resample draws across scenarios (common random
   137	  numbers). Percentile 95% intervals; if a statistic is degenerate
   138	  (all-0/all-1), report the exact one-sided CP bound at the target level
   139	  instead. Pooled exact McNemar is PROHIBITED for D2; use the target-cluster
   140	  paired-difference bootstrap.
   141	- Sensitivity contrasts (D2 ladder, phase draws, amplitude-stationarity):
   142	  COMMON-SUBSET RULE — every contrast against nominal is computed with
   143	  nominal re-evaluated on the same median-window (K=1) subset and the same
   144	  bootstrap draws. Min-max across the 3x3 grid is a "prespecified
   145	  finite-grid sensitivity range", never a confidence band; endpoint
